      "body": "ACK [0574f09](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/36636/commits/0574f096abf0cfe75501542efe1787679340d3d3)\r\n\r\nOne non-blocking nit \r\n`ToLower(addr.substr(...))` creates a temporary `std::string` (though 6 chars fits within SSO). \r\nUsing `CaseInsensitiveEqual(addr.substr(addr.size() - suffix.size()), suffix)` from `util/strencodings.h` avoids the temporary string entirely. \r\nIt would be nice to use that here (and similarly in SetI2P()) for consistency, ",
